   "avy_zone": null,
   "blurb": "The left ice cliff is the busiest ice sector on Montagne du Tranchant in Lanaudière, a cliff described as the most popular in the region. About a dozen winter lines are found here, nearly all water ice from WI2 up to a single WI5, with the bulk around WI3, plus one mixed route near M7. A footpath through the woods on the left side leads to the top of several routes, which makes building top-rope anchors straightforward and suits climbers developing their ice skills. Expect company on good days, and wear a helmet at the base.",
